                "url": "https://www.math.uchicago.edu/~may/CONCISE/ConciseRevised.pdf"
              }
            ]
          },
          "statement": "Assume AC. On finite CW pairs the Bott-compatible Omega-prespectrum KU represents the locally defined complex K^* groups. After Bott translation to q<=-2, ku->KU identifies the E3 source, target and d3. At (p,q), p>=1, this d3 is the cellular obstruction from the Postnikov layer of ku_(p+q) joining pi_p=pi_(-q)ku to pi_(p+2)=pi_(2-q)ku, the corresponding Bott translate of the first stable ku invariant.",
          "title": "KU representability and the skeletal–Postnikov d-three comparison"
        },
