            "proof": "not-applicable"
          },
          "sources": {
            "references": [
              {
                "title": "Jean Gallier, Clifford Algebras, Clifford Groups, and a Generalization of the Quaternions: The Pin and Spin Groups, §1.2",
                "url": "https://arxiv.org/pdf/0805.0311"
              },
              {
                "title": "M. F. Atiyah, R. Bott, and A. Shapiro, Clifford Modules, Part I, §1",
                "url": "https://www.math.ens.psl.eu/~benoist/refs/ABS.pdf"
              }
            ]
          },
          "definition": "Let $k$ be a field with $\\operatorname{char}(k)\\ne2$, let $V$ be a finite-dimensional $k$-vector space, and let $B:V\\times V\\to k$ be a symmetric bilinear form, not necessarily nondegenerate. Put $Q(v)=B(v,v)$. Write $T_k(V)$ for the tensor algebra and $j:V\\to T_k(V)$ for its degree-one inclusion ([[def-tensor-algebra-of-a-vector-space]]). For each $v\\in V$, set $r_v=j(v)j(v)-Q(v)1$ and let $J_Q$ be the intersection of all two-sided ideals of $T_k(V)$ containing every $r_v$ ([[def-left-right-and-two-sided-ideal]]). This family is nonempty because it contains $T_k(V)$, and its intersection is a two-sided ideal; thus $J_Q$ is the smallest such ideal.\n\nDefine the **universal Clifford algebra** with the plus-$Q$ convention by\n\n$$\\mathrm{Cl}^{+}(V,Q):=T_k(V)/J_Q.$$\n\nThe quotient operations are induced from $T_k(V)$; the two-sided ideal condition makes multiplication of cosets well defined. Let $q_Q:T_k(V)\\to\\mathrm{Cl}^{+}(V,Q)$ be the quotient map, put $i_Q=q_Q\\circ j$, and write $\\bar v=i_Q(v)$. The defining relation is $\\bar v^{\\,2}=Q(v)1$. In this pair, $\\mathrm{Cl}(V,Q)$ abbreviates $\\mathrm{Cl}^{+}(V,Q)$ after this sign convention has been fixed. No nondegeneracy assumption is imposed.",
          "status": "draft"
        },
        {
          "id": "lem-clifford-exterior-wedge-contraction-relations",
          "kind": "lemma",
          "page": "clifford-universal-algebras-and-pbw",
          "dependency_level": 0,
          "title": "Wedge and contraction operators satisfy the Clifford relations",
          "deps": [
