            "def-exterior-algebra-of-a-finite-free-module",
            "cor-finite-iterated-tensor-products-represent-multilinear-maps",
            "def-left-right-and-two-sided-ideal"
          ],
          "justified_by": [],
          "proof_strategy": "direct",
          "provenance": {
            "statement": "literature-derived",
            "proof": "ai-altered"
          },
          "sources": {
            "references": [
              {
                "title": "Eckhard Meinrenken, Clifford algebras and Lie groups, lecture notes, Chapter 2, §1.2 (15)–(16) and §2.1 Proposition 2.2, printed pp. 24–25",
                "url": "https://www.math.toronto.edu/mein/teaching/LieClifford/cl12.pdf"
              }
            ]
          },
          "statement": "Let $k$ be a field of characteristic not $2$, let $V$ be a finite-dimensional $k$-vector space, and let $B:V\\times V\\to k$ be symmetric bilinear, possibly degenerate. Set $Q(v)=B(v,v)$ and let $\\Lambda V$ be the exterior algebra of the finite free $k$-module $V$ ([[def-exterior-algebra-of-a-finite-free-module]]). Define $\\epsilon_v(\\omega)=v\\wedge\\omega$ and, on decomposable wedges,\n\n$$\\iota_v(w_1\\wedge\\cdots\\wedge w_r)=\\sum_{j=1}^r(-1)^{j-1}B(v,w_j)\\,w_1\\wedge\\cdots\\wedge\\widehat{w_j}\\wedge\\cdots\\wedge w_r,$$\n\nwith $\\iota_v(1)=0$. Then $\\iota_v$ is well defined and $k$-linear, and the operators $c(v)=\\epsilon_v+\\iota_v$ satisfy $c(v)^2=Q(v)I_{\\Lambda V}$ for every $v\\in V$, where $I_{\\Lambda V}$ is the identity map on $\\Lambda V$.",
          "status": "draft"
        },
        {
          "id": "lem-clifford-polarized-relations",
          "kind": "lemma",
          "page": "clifford-universal-algebras-and-pbw",
          "dependency_level": 1,
          "title": "Polarized relations in a Clifford algebra",
          "deps": [
