        {
          "id": "def-rank-one-heisenberg-vertex-algebra",
          "kind": "definition",
          "title": "Rank-one Heisenberg oscillator fields and vacuum space",
          "deps": [
            "def-polynomial-ring-on-a-family-of-indeterminates",
            "def-formal-distribution-on-a-vector-space"
          ],
          "dependency_level": 1,
          "statement": "Let $P=\\mathbb C[x_1,x_2,\\ldots]$ be the polynomial algebra whose elements involve finitely many indeterminates, as in [[def-polynomial-ring-on-a-family-of-indeterminates]]. Give $x_r$ degree $r$ and write $P_d$ for its degree-$d$ subspace. On $P$, put\n\n$$a_{-r}=x_r\\cdot,\\qquad a_r=r\\frac{\\partial}{\\partial x_r}\\quad(r\\ge1),\\qquad a_0=0,\\qquad \\mathbf1=1,\\qquad T=\\sum_{r\\ge1}r x_{r+1}\\frac{\\partial}{\\partial x_r}.$$\n\nEvery sum of operators here is applied to a polynomial and is then finite. Define $a(z)=\\sum_{n\\in\\mathbb Z}a_nz^{-n-1}$, in the conventions of [[def-formal-distribution-on-a-vector-space]], and the divided derivative $b_r(z)=\\partial_z^{r-1}a(z)/(r-1)!$ for $r\\ge1$. In normal ordering, all modes $a_n$ with $n<0$ are moved to the left of all modes with $n\\ge0$, preserving their respective internal orders. For a polynomial monomial $v=x_{r_1}\\cdots x_{r_s}$ define the candidate field\n\n$$Y(v,z)={:}b_{r_1}(z)\\cdots b_{r_s}(z){:},\\qquad Y(1,z)=I.$$\n\nThe empty normal product is the identity. The same-sign modes commute, so the formula is symmetric in the listed factors; it is extended linearly from the polynomial monomial basis. Set $\\omega=\\tfrac12 x_1^2$. The well-defined state-field and conformal-VOA structure on this vacuum space are proved in [[thm-rank-one-heisenberg-vertex-operator-algebra]]. The symbol $a_n$ is a current mode; in particular $Y(x_1,z)=a(z)$ and $Y(\\omega,z)=\\sum_nL(n)z^{-n-2}$ use different mode shifts.",
          "axiom_use": "None; explicit polynomial monomial bases, finite matching sums and degreewise formal calculations.",
          "provenance": {
            "statement": "literature-derived",
            "proof": "not-applicable"
          },
          "justified_by": [
            "thm-rank-one-heisenberg-vertex-operator-algebra"
          ],
          "sources": [
            {
              "title": "Tomoyuki Arakawa and Anne Moreau, Arc Spaces and Vertex Algebras",
              "url": "https://www.imo.universite-paris-saclay.fr/~anne.moreau/Arc_space-vertex_algebras-BOOK_version.pdf"
            },
            {
              "title": "Christophe Nozaradan, Introduction to Vertex Algebras",
              "url": "https://arxiv.org/pdf/0809.1380"
