        {
          "id": "thm-rank-one-heisenberg-vertex-operator-algebra",
          "kind": "theorem",
          "title": "The rank-one Heisenberg vacuum space is a conformal VOA of central charge one",
          "deps": [
            "def-rank-one-heisenberg-vertex-algebra",
            "lem-state-field-reconstruction-from-local-generators",
            "def-conformal-vertex-algebra",
            "def-vertex-algebra-state-field",
            "def-formal-distribution-on-a-vector-space"
          ],
          "dependency_level": 4,
          "statement": "The data in [[def-rank-one-heisenberg-vertex-algebra]] define a vertex algebra with the displayed normal-monomial state fields. With $\\omega=\\tfrac12x_1^2$ it is a conformal vertex algebra of CFT type in the convention of [[def-conformal-vertex-algebra]], with central charge $1$. Its conformal modes are\n\n$$L(n)=\\frac12\\sum_{k\\in\\mathbb Z}{:}a_k a_{n-k}{:},\\qquad L(0)=\\sum_{r\\ge1}r x_r\\frac{\\partial}{\\partial x_r},\\qquad L(-1)=T.$$\n\nEach quadratic-mode sum is finite on every vector. The weight-$d$ space is $P_d$, with the finite basis of monomials $\\prod_r x_r^{m_r}$ satisfying $\\sum_r r m_r=d$; in particular $P_0=\\mathbb C\\mathbf1$.",
          "axiom_use": "None; explicit polynomial monomial bases, finite matching sums and degreewise formal calculations.",
          "provenance": {
            "statement": "literature-derived",
            "proof": "ai-altered"
          },
          "sources": [
            {
              "title": "Tomoyuki Arakawa and Anne Moreau, Arc Spaces and Vertex Algebras",
