        {
          "id": "lem-heisenberg-normal-ordered-fields-satisfy-module-jacobi",
          "kind": "lemma",
          "title": "Heisenberg normal-ordered fields give modules with an arbitrary zero-mode action",
          "deps": [
            "def-rank-one-heisenberg-vertex-algebra",
            "thm-rank-one-heisenberg-vertex-operator-algebra",
            "def-vertex-algebra-module",
            "lem-module-jacobi-formal-delta-substitution-identity",
            "def-formal-distribution-on-a-vector-space",
            "def-admissible-vertex-algebra-module"
          ],
          "dependency_level": 5,
          "statement": "Let $V=P$ be the rank-one Heisenberg vertex algebra of [[thm-rank-one-heisenberg-vertex-operator-algebra]]. For any complex vector space $E$ and any $A\\in\\operatorname{End}_{\\mathbb C}(E)$, set $F(E,A)=P\\otimes E$ and define\n\n$$a_{-r}=x_r\\cdot\\otimes I_E,\\qquad a_r=r\\partial_{x_r}\\otimes I_E\\ (r\\ge1),\\qquad a_0=I_P\\otimes A.$$\n\nWrite $a^F(z)=\\sum_na_nz^{-n-1}$ and $b_r^F(z)=\\partial_z^{r-1}a^F(z)/(r-1)!$. With the same negative/nonnegative-mode normal ordering as [[def-rank-one-heisenberg-vertex-algebra]], put\n\n$$Y_F(x_{r_1}\\cdots x_{r_s},z)={:}b_{r_1}^F(z)\\cdots b_{r_s}^F(z){:},\\qquad Y_F(1,z)=I.$$\n\nThese fields give a $V$-module in the full formal-Jacobi convention of [[def-vertex-algebra-module]]. In particular, no diagonalizability or nilpotence condition on $A$ is required. For $v\\in P_w$ and $f\\in P_d\\otimes E$, each mode satisfies\n\n$$v^F_{(k)}f\\in P_{d+w-k-1}\\otimes E,$$\n\nwhere negative degrees are zero. Thus the fields are lower truncated, and this is an admissible nonnegative integer grading whenever the module is viewed over the conformal VOA. No logarithmic powers occur in $Y_F$ itself.",
          "axiom_use": "None; explicit polynomial monomial bases, finite matching sums and degreewise formal calculations.",
          "provenance": {
