        },
        {
          "id": "thm-rank-one-heisenberg-jordan-fock-module",
          "kind": "theorem",
          "title": "The Heisenberg Jordan Fock family is grading-restricted; it is logarithmic exactly when λ is nonzero",
          "deps": [
            "lem-heisenberg-normal-ordered-fields-satisfy-module-jacobi",
            "thm-rank-one-heisenberg-vertex-operator-algebra",
            "def-admissible-vertex-algebra-module",
            "def-grading-restricted-generalized-vertex-module",
            "def-ordinary-vertex-module",
            "def-logarithmic-vertex-module"
          ],
          "dependency_level": 6,
          "statement": "Let $E=\\mathbb C e_0\\oplus\\mathbb C e_1$, define $Ne_0=0$, $Ne_1=e_0$, and let $A_\\lambda=\\lambda I+N$ for $\\lambda\\in\\mathbb C$. The oscillator module $F_\\lambda=F(E,A_\\lambda)$ constructed in [[lem-heisenberg-normal-ordered-fields-satisfy-module-jacobi]] is a module over the conformal CFT-type rank-one Heisenberg VOA of central charge $1$. Its conformal modes are\n\n$$L_F(n)=\\frac12\\sum_{k\\in\\mathbb Z}{:}a_k a_{n-k}{:},\\qquad L_F(0)=D\\otimes I_E+\\tfrac12 I_P\\otimes A_\\lambda^2=D\\otimes I_E+\\tfrac{\\lambda^2}{2}I+\\lambda I_P\\otimes N,$$\n\nwhere $D|_{P_d}=dI$. The degree spaces $P_d\\otimes E$ give an admissible grading and are exactly the generalized weight spaces of weights $d+\\lambda^2/2$, of dimension $2\\dim P_d$. Thus $F_\\lambda$ is grading-restricted generalized. It is logarithmic exactly when $\\lambda\\ne0$; at $\\lambda=0$ it is ordinary despite its nonsemisimple current zero mode. In particular $F_1$ has $a_0=I+N$ and $L_F(0)|_E=\\tfrac12I+N$.",
          "axiom_use": "None; explicit polynomial monomial bases, finite matching sums and degreewise formal calculations.",
          "provenance": {
