      "items": [
        {
          "id": "def-hall-finitary-abelian-category",
          "kind": "definition",
          "title": "Small finitary abelian categories for Hall multiplication",
          "deps": [
            "def-small-locally-small-and-large-category",
            "def-abelian-category",
            "def-exact-sequence-and-short-exact-sequence-in-an-abelian-category",
            "def-extension-of-an-object-by-an-object-in-an-abelian-category",
            "def-n-fold-yoneda-extension",
            "def-subobject-and-quotient-object",
            "def-the-quotient-of-an-object-by-a-subobject",
            "def-equivalence-of-n-fold-extensions"
          ],
          "dependency_level": 0,
          "justified_by": [],
          "provenance": {
            "statement": "literature-derived",
            "proof": "not-applicable"
          },
          "sources": {
            "references": [
              {
                "title": "Olivier Schiffmann, Lectures on Hall Algebras, arXiv:math/0611617v2, §§1.1 and 1.3",
                "url": "https://arxiv.org/pdf/math/0611617v2"
              },
              {
                "title": "Matthew B. Young, Degenerate versions of Green’s theorem for Hall modules, arXiv:1810.08238v2, §2.1",
                "url": "https://arxiv.org/pdf/1810.08238v2"
              }
            ]
          },
          "statement": "A **small finitary abelian category** for Hall multiplication is a small\nabelian category $\\mathcal A$ (its object and morphism collections are sets,\nby [[def-small-locally-small-and-large-category]]), with abelian structure as\nin [[def-abelian-category]], in which the\nfollowing sets are finite for every pair of objects $M,N$:\n\n1. $\\operatorname{Hom}_{\\mathcal A}(M,N)$;\n2. $\\operatorname{YExt}^{1}_{\\mathcal A}(M,N)$, the set of Yoneda classes of\n   short exact sequences $0\\to N\\to E\\to M\\to0$. Equivalence is the\n   one-fold instance of the generated endpoint-fixed chain-map relation in\n   [[def-equivalence-of-n-fold-extensions]]: chain maps are the identity on\n   $N$ and $M$, and the relation is closed under reflexivity, symmetry and\n   transitivity. A short exact sequence and its endpoint order use\n   [[def-exact-sequence-and-short-exact-sequence-in-an-abelian-category]],\n   [[def-extension-of-an-object-by-an-object-in-an-abelian-category]] and\n   [[def-n-fold-yoneda-extension]].\n\nOne may instead supply a small skeleton $\\mathcal A_0$ of an essentially\nsmall abelian category and perform the construction on $\\mathcal A_0$. Here\n“essentially small” means that such a small equivalent category is part of the\ngiven data; the construction does not select representatives by an unstated\nchoice principle. The isomorphism classes $\\operatorname{Iso}(\\mathcal A_0)$\nthen form a set.\n\nNo $\\mathbb F_q$-linear structure, enough projectives or injectives, finite\nnumber of subobjects of every object, or identification with derived\n$\\operatorname{Ext}^{1}$ is included in this definition. Subobjects are the\nmonomorphism classes of [[def-subobject-and-quotient-object]], and quotients\nare the cokernels specified in [[def-the-quotient-of-an-object-by-a-subobject]].",
          "source_path": "items/def-hall-finitary-abelian-category.md"
        },
        {
          "id": "lem-hall-flags-lift-through-a-quotient",
          "kind": "lemma",
          "title": "Flags lift uniquely through a quotient in an abelian category",
          "deps": [
            "def-abelian-category",
            "def-subobject-and-quotient-object",
            "def-the-quotient-of-an-object-by-a-subobject",
            "def-the-direct-image-and-inverse-image-of-a-subobject",
            "thm-direct-and-inverse-image-of-subobjects-form-a-galois-connection",
            "thm-the-pullback-of-an-epimorphism-is-an-epimorphism",
            "thm-first-isomorphism-theorem-in-an-abelian-category",
            "thm-third-isomorphism-theorem-in-an-abelian-category",
            "thm-every-monomorphism-is-the-kernel-of-its-cokernel"
