          },
          "statement": "Let $k=\\mathbb F_q$, and let $I_\\lambda$ denote the nilpotent Jordan-quiver\nrepresentation indexed by a partition $\\lambda$, as in\n[[lem-jordan-quiver-isoclasses-are-partition-indexed]]. For partitions\n$\\mu,\\nu,\\lambda$, let $g^\\lambda_{\\mu,\\nu}(q)$ be the coefficient of\n$[I_\\lambda]$ in the untwisted product $[I_\\mu]*[I_\\nu]$. There are\npolynomials $G^\\lambda_{\\mu,\\nu}(t)\\in\\mathbb Z[t]$, independent of the\nfinite field, with\n$$ g^\\lambda_{\\mu,\\nu}(q)=G^\\lambda_{\\mu,\\nu}(q). $$\nA coefficient is zero unless $|\\lambda|=|\\mu|+|\\nu|$.\n\nDefine the **generic Jordan-quiver Hall algebra** by\n$$ H_{\\mathrm{gen}}:=\\bigoplus_\\lambda\\mathbb Z[t]u_\\lambda, \\qquad u_\\mu*u_\\nu:=\\sum_\\lambda G^\\lambda_{\\mu,\\nu}(t)u_\\lambda, $$\ngiving $u_\\lambda$ degree $|\\lambda|$ and $t$ degree $0$.\nThe size condition above makes this a graded algebra.\nThen $H_{\\mathrm{gen}}$ is a commutative associative unital algebra and a free\npolynomial algebra over $\\mathbb Z[t]$ on the classes\n$u_{(1^r)}$, $r\\ge1$. After extending scalars to\n$\\mathbb Z[t,t^{-1}]$, the assignment\n$$ \\Phi_t(u_{(1^r)})=t^{-r(r-1)/2}e_r $$\nfor every $r\\ge1$, and $\\Phi_t(u_\\varnothing)=1$, extends uniquely to a\ngraded algebra isomorphism\n$$ H_{\\mathrm{gen}}\\otimes_{\\mathbb Z[t]}\\mathbb Z[t,t^{-1}] \\;\\cong\\; \\Lambda\\otimes_{\\mathbb Z}\\mathbb Z[t,t^{-1}], $$\nwhere $\\Lambda$ is the stable graded ring of symmetric functions.",
