          "sources": {
            "references": [
              {
                "title": "Olivier Schiffmann, Lectures on Hall Algebras, arXiv:math/0611617v2",
                "url": "https://arxiv.org/pdf/math/0611617v2"
              },
              {
                "title": "Claus Michael Ringel, Hall algebras and quantum groups, Inventiones Mathematicae 101 (1990), 583–591",
                "url": "https://noah.nrw/ubbihs/download/pdf/5112433",
                "locator": "§1, printed pp. 585–586: composition-algebra flag counts (background only). The Green coproduct and tensor conventions are from Schiffmann §§1.4–1.5, cited above."
              }
            ]
          },
          "statement": "Let $\\mathcal A$ be a finite-field hereditary Hall category and use\n$H_{\\mathcal A,\\nu}$ and the object-level integer $\\chi_0(M,N)$ from\n[[def-euler-twisted-hall-algebra]]. For a basis object $R$, let\n$P^R_{M,N}$ count endpoint-labelled exact sequences\n$0\\to N\\to R\\to M\\to0$, and put $a_R=|\\operatorname{Aut}(R)|$. Define the\n**coefficientwise completed tensor space**\n$$ H_{\\mathcal A,\\nu}\\widehat\\otimes H_{\\mathcal A,\\nu} =\\prod_{([M],[N])}\\mathbb Q(\\nu)\\,([M]\\otimes[N]), $$\nthe space of all coefficient functions on ordered pairs of isomorphism\nclasses. Define the Green coproduct and counit by\n$$ \\Delta'([R])=\\sum_{[M],[N]} \\nu^{\\chi_0(M,N)}\\frac{P^R_{M,N}}{a_R}[M]\\otimes[N], \\qquad \\epsilon([R])=\\begin{cases}1,&R\\cong0,\\\\0,&R\\not\\cong0.\\end{cases} $$\nEach coefficient is finite; the sum need not have finite support. On finite\npure tensors define the **Euler-twisted tensor multiplication** by\n$$ ([X]\\otimes[Y])\\cdot([Z]\\otimes[W]) =\\nu^{\\chi_0(Y,Z)+\\chi_0(Z,Y)}([X]\\star[Z])\\otimes([Y]\\star[W]). $$\nIt is extended to completed tensors only when every output coefficient is a\nfinite sum. No algebra structure on the whole completion is asserted; this\nfinite-convergence condition is proved for products of Green images below.",
          "source_path": "items/def-green-hall-completion-and-coproduct.md"
        },
