        {
          "id": "lem-green-cross-square-counting-identity",
          "kind": "lemma",
          "title": "The Green cross–square counting identity",
          "deps": [
            "def-finite-field-hereditary-hall-category",
            "lem-yext-exact-sequences-in-both-variables",
            "def-abelian-category",
            "def-pullback-and-pushout-of-an-extension"
          ],
          "dependency_level": 2,
          "justified_by": [],
          "provenance": {
            "statement": "literature-derived",
            "proof": "ai-altered"
          },
          "sources": {
            "references": [
              {
                "title": "Olivier Schiffmann, Lectures on Hall Algebras, arXiv:math/0611617v2",
                "url": "https://arxiv.org/pdf/math/0611617v2"
              },
              {
                "title": "Matthew B. Young, Degenerate versions of Green’s theorem for Hall modules, arXiv:1810.08238v2",
                "url": "https://arxiv.org/pdf/1810.08238v2"
              },
              {
                "title": "Claus Michael Ringel, Hall algebras and quantum groups, Inventiones Mathematicae 101 (1990), 583–591",
                "url": "https://noah.nrw/ubbihs/download/pdf/5112433",
                "locator": "§§1–2, printed pp. 585–588: composition-algebra flag counts and Serre relations (background only). The cross–square identity is proved locally following Schiffmann §1.5, cited above."
              }
            ]
          },
          "statement": "Let $\\mathcal A$ be a finite-field hereditary Hall category. Write\n$a_X=|\\operatorname{Aut}(X)|$, and let $P^R_{M,N}$ count exact sequences\n$0\\to N\\to R\\to M\\to0$. For fixed objects $M,N,K,L$, the following\ncross–square identity holds:\n$$ \\sum_{[J]}\\frac{P^J_{M,N}P^J_{K,L}}{a_J} =\\sum_{[K_1],[K_2],[L_1],[L_2]} \\frac{|\\operatorname{YExt}^1(K_2,L_1)|} {|\\operatorname{Hom}(K_2,L_1)|} \\frac{P^K_{K_2,K_1}P^L_{L_2,L_1}P^M_{K_2,L_2}P^N_{K_1,L_1}} {a_{K_1}a_{K_2}a_{L_1}a_{L_2}}. $$\nBoth sums are finite. The left side counts pairs of exact sequences with a\ncommon middle object $J$; the right side counts the compatible four-edge\nsquare data, weighted by the displayed Yoneda Ext/Hom ratio.\n\nThe diagrams below display the data being counted. A **cross** is a pair of\nshort exact sequences with the same middle object; it is not an assertion of\nvertical maps between the endpoint objects.\n\n```tikzcd\n0 \\arrow[r] & N \\arrow[r, tail, \"n\"] & J \\arrow[r, two heads, \"b\"] & M \\arrow[r] & 0 \\\\\n0 \\arrow[r] & L \\arrow[r, tail, \"\\ell\"] & J \\arrow[r, two heads, \"b'\"] & K \\arrow[r] & 0\n```\n\nA **square datum** is the isomorphism class of these four exact edges:\n$$ 0\\to L_1\\to N\\to K_1\\to0, \\quad 0\\to L_1\\to L\\to L_2\\to0, \\quad 0\\to K_1\\to K\\to K_2\\to0, \\quad 0\\to L_2\\to M\\to K_2\\to0. $$\n\n```tikzcd\n0 \\arrow[r] & L_1 \\arrow[r, tail] \\arrow[d, equal] & N \\arrow[r, two heads] & K_1 \\arrow[r] & 0 \\\\\n0 \\arrow[r] & L_1 \\arrow[r, tail] & L \\arrow[r, two heads] & L_2 \\arrow[r] & 0\n\\\\[1.2em]\n0 \\arrow[r] & K_1 \\arrow[r, tail] & K \\arrow[r, two heads] \\arrow[d, equal] & K_2 \\arrow[r] & 0 \\\\\n0 \\arrow[r] & L_2 \\arrow[r, tail] & M \\arrow[r, two heads] & K_2 \\arrow[r] & 0\n```\n\nThe equal labels indicate shared endpoint isomorphism classes only; no\nadditional morphisms between the two rows are part of the square datum.",
          "source_path": "items/lem-green-cross-square-counting-identity.md",
          "proof_strategy": "direct",
          "strategy": "Take kernels, images, and cokernels in each cross, then count completions by the Yoneda exact sequence and explicit automorphism stabilizers."
        },
