          },
          "statement": "Let $\\mathcal A$ be a finite-field hereditary Hall category and let\n$K_0=K_0(\\mathcal A)$. Put\n$([\\alpha],[\\beta])=\\langle\\alpha,\\beta\\rangle+\n\\langle\\beta,\\alpha\\rangle$. The **extended Hall algebra** is the vector\nspace $\\widetilde H=\\mathbb Q(\\nu)[K_0]\\otimes H_{\\mathcal A,\\nu}$ with\nbasis $k_\\alpha[M]$ and multiplication\n$$ (k_\\alpha[M])(k_\\beta[N]) =\\nu^{-(\\beta,[M])}k_{\\alpha+\\beta}([M]\\star[N]). $$\nThe notation is left-torus normal order: $k_\\alpha[M]$ is the actual product of the torus and Hall elements. Thus moving $k_\\beta$ past $[M]$ contributes $\\nu^{-(\\beta,[M])}$. Equivalently, $k_\\alpha k_\\beta=k_{\\alpha+\\beta}$ and\n$k_\\alpha[M]k_\\alpha^{-1}=\\nu^{(\\alpha,[M])}[M]$. Associativity follows\nfrom the bilinearity of the symmetric Euler form and the associative Hall\nproduct; the toral action is checked in\n[[lem-extended-hall-torus-action-is-well-defined]].\n\nIf $\\mathcal A$ has a specified set of simple objects $\\{S_i\\}$, the\n**composition subalgebra** is the subalgebra of $H_{\\mathcal A,\\nu}$\ngenerated by $[S_i]$. Its extension by all $k_\\alpha$ is the **extended\ncomposition subalgebra**.",
          "source_path": "items/def-extended-hall-algebra-and-composition-subalgebra.md"
        },
