          "statement": "Let $I$ be finite, $A=(a_{jk})$ a symmetric generalized Cartan matrix, and $q>0$ a real number with $q\\ne1$. Let $S$ be the complex associative algebra on generators $e_j$ for $j\\in I$, with only the numerical quantum Serre relations\n$$ \\sum_{s=0}^{N+1}(-1)^s{N+1\\brack s}_q e_j^{N+1-s}e_ke_j^s=0,\\qquad j\\ne k,\\quad N=-a_{jk}. $$\nHere $[r]_q=(q^r-q^{-r})/(q-q^{-1})$, divided powers are $e_j^{(n)}=e_j^n/[n]_q!$, and $S$ is graded by $\\deg e_j=\\alpha_j$. Fix $i\\in I$ and write $m(\\beta)=\\sum_j a_{ij}\\beta_j$ for a root degree $\\beta=\\sum_j\\beta_j\\alpha_j$.\n\nThe operators on words specified by\n$$ D(e_j)=D'(e_j)=\\delta_{ij},\\quad D(xy)=D(x)y+q^{m(\\deg x)}xD(y),\\quad D'(xy)=q^{m(\\deg y)}D'(x)y+xD'(y) $$\ndescend to $S$, commute, and are locally nilpotent. Set $B_i=\\ker D$. Then\n$$ S=\\bigoplus_{n\\geq0}e_i^{(n)}B_i. $$\nFor homogeneous $b\\in B_i$ put\n$$ R(b)=e_i b-q^{-m(\\deg b)}b e_i,\\qquad F(b)=-\\frac{D'(b)}{q-q^{-1}},\\qquad K(b)=q^{m(\\deg b)}b. $$\nThese define an integrable type-one $U_q(\\mathfrak{sl}_2)$ action on $B_i$, with conventions $KRK^{-1}=q^2R$, $KFK^{-1}=q^{-2}F$, and $RF-FR=(K-K^{-1})/(q-q^{-1})$. The algebra $B_i$ is generated by the finite root strings $R^r(e_j)$, $j\\ne i$, $0\\leq r\\leq-a_{ij}$. In particular, if $0\\ne z\\in S_\\beta$ satisfies $D(z)=D'(z)=0$, then $m(\\beta)\\leq0$.",
