          },
          "source_path": "items/thm-hall-algebra-regular-module.md",
          "proof_strategy": "direct",
          "statement": "Let $R$ be a commutative ring with unit, and let $H$ be any unital associative\n$R$-algebra that is a Hall algebra. The map\n$\\rho:H\\to\\operatorname{End}_R(H)$ given by $\\rho(a)(h)=ah$ is a\nrepresentation, so the left regular action makes $H$ a Hall-algebra module."
