        {
          "id": "ex-a1-nakajima-hecke-correspondence-as-fundamental-sl2-module",
          "kind": "example",
          "title": "The A1 Nakajima correspondence in the fundamental sl2 representation",
          "deps": [
            "def-a1-nakajima-framed-quiver-data",
            "lem-a1-nakajima-varieties-and-hecke-correspondence-are-points",
            "thm-a1-nakajima-hecke-correspondence-gives-sl2-action"
          ],
          "dependency_level": 3,
          "justified_by": [],
          "provenance": {
            "statement": "literature-derived",
            "proof": "ai-altered"
          },
          "sources": {
            "references": [
              {
                "title": "Hiraku Nakajima, Introduction to quiver varieties—for ring and representation theorists, §§4.2, 4.4–4.5",
                "url": "https://arxiv.org/pdf/1611.10000"
              }
            ]
          },
          "source_path": "items/ex-a1-nakajima-hecke-correspondence-as-fundamental-sl2-module.md",
          "proof_strategy": "direct",
          "statement": "For the one-vertex, no-arrow quiver with framing dimension one, the two\nnonempty Nakajima fibres are points at $v=0$ and $v=1$. On their fundamental\nclasses $e_0,e_1$, the Hecke correspondence gives\n$$E=\\begin{pmatrix}0&1\\\\0&0\\end{pmatrix},\\qquad F=\\begin{pmatrix}0&0\\\\1&0\\end{pmatrix},\\qquad H=\\begin{pmatrix}1&0\\\\0&-1\\end{pmatrix}.$$"
        },
        {
          "id": "ex-two-distinct-one-dimensional-modules-over-generic-jordan-hall-algebra",
          "kind": "example",
          "title": "Two distinct one-dimensional modules over the generic Jordan Hall algebra",
          "deps": [
            "def-hall-algebra-module",
            "thm-generic-jordan-hall-algebra-is-symmetric-functions"
          ],
          "dependency_level": 5,
          "justified_by": [],
          "provenance": {
            "statement": "literature-derived",
            "proof": "ai-altered"
          },
          "sources": {
            "references": [
              {
                "title": "Olivier Schiffmann, Lectures on Hall Algebras, arXiv:math/0611617v2, §2.3",
                "url": "https://arxiv.org/pdf/math/0611617v2"
              }
            ]
          },
          "source_path": "items/ex-two-distinct-one-dimensional-modules-over-generic-jordan-hall-algebra.md",
          "proof_strategy": "direct",
          "statement": "Let $K=\\mathbb Q(t)$ and let $H_{J,K}$ be the generic Jordan Hall algebra.\nBy [[thm-generic-jordan-hall-algebra-is-symmetric-functions]],\n$H_{J,K}=K[u_1,u_2,\\ldots]$ as an algebra, where $u_r$ is the generator\ncorresponding to the class $u_{(1^r)}$. The assignments\n$$\\epsilon_0(u_r)=0\\quad(r\\ge1),\\qquad \\epsilon_1(u_1)=1,\\quad\\epsilon_1(u_r)=0\\quad(r\\ge2)$$\ngive two different one-dimensional Hall modules on the same $K$-vector\nspace $K$, by $h\\cdot z=\\epsilon_i(h)z$."
        },
        {
          "id": "ex-degree-one-green-pairing-normalization-of-jordan-fock-action",
          "kind": "example",
          "title": "Degree-one normalization for the Jordan Hall Green pairing and Fock action",
          "deps": [
            "thm-jordan-quiver-hall-module-realizes-normalized-heisenberg-fock-action",
            "thm-jordan-hall-pairing-and-hall-littlewood-basis",
            "def-hall-inner-product-on-symmetric-functions",
            "cor-power-sums-are-orthogonal-for-the-hall-inner-product"
          ],
          "dependency_level": 7,
          "justified_by": [],
          "provenance": {
            "statement": "literature-derived",
            "proof": "ai-altered"
          },
          "sources": {
            "references": [
              {
                "title": "Olivier Schiffmann, Lectures on Hall Algebras, arXiv:math/0611617v2, §2.4, equation (2.9)",
                "url": "https://arxiv.org/pdf/math/0611617v2"
              },
              {
                "title": "I. G. Macdonald, Symmetric Functions and Hall Polynomials, 2nd ed., Chapter I §4, equations (4.5)–(4.7) and Remark 8",
                "url": "https://math.berkeley.edu/~corteel/MATH249/macdonald.pdf"
              }
            ]
          },
          "source_path": "items/ex-degree-one-green-pairing-normalization-of-jordan-fock-action.md",
          "proof_strategy": "direct",
          "statement": "For $p_1^r$ ($r\\ge0$), the ordinary symmetric-function Hall form has norm\n$\\langle p_1^r,p_1^r\\rangle_H=r!$, while the transported Jordan Green\npairing has norm $(p_1^r,p_1^r)_G=r!(t-1)^{-r}$. If $X_1$ is multiplication\nby $p_1$, its adjoints therefore satisfy\n$$X_1^{\\dagger,H}p_1^r=r p_1^{r-1},\\qquad X_1^{\\dagger,G}p_1^r=\\frac{r}{t-1}p_1^{r-1}\\quad(r\\ge1),$$\nand the normalized Fock operator $P_1=(t-1)X_1^{\\dagger,G}$ has the usual\nderivative action $P_1p_1^r=r p_1^{r-1}$; both adjoints kill $1$.\nHere $X_1^\\dagger$ denotes the adjoint characterized by\n$\\langle X_1f,g\\rangle=\\langle f,X_1^\\dagger g\\rangle$ for the indicated\nbilinear form; the diagonal nonzero power-sum norms make these adjoints\nwell-defined degree by degree."
        }
      ],
      "scaffold": "research/plan-physics-algebras-track.md",
      "order": 2921
    }

{
      "id": "motivic-hall-algebras-and-integration",
      "title": "Motivic Hall Algebras and Integration Maps",
      "kind": "A",
      "category": "hall-algebras-and-tensor-categories",
      "label": "PA-23-A",
      "companion": "motivic-hall-algebras-and-integration-examples",
      "requires": [
        "finitary-ringel-hall-algebras",
        "derived-hall-algebras",
