            "def-motivic-hall-algebra-of-a-finite-quiver"
          ],
          "dependency_level": 2,
          "justified_by": [],
          "provenance": {
            "statement": "literature-derived",
            "proof": "not-applicable"
          },
          "sources": {
            "references": [
              {
                "title": "Tom Bridgeland, An Introduction to Motivic Hall Algebras, arXiv:1002.4372v1, §§4.3 and 5.2",
                "url": "https://arxiv.org/pdf/1002.4372v1"
              },
              {
                "title": "Olivier Schiffmann, Lectures on Hall Algebras, arXiv:math/0611617v2, §§1.2–1.3",
                "url": "https://arxiv.org/pdf/math/0611617v2"
              }
            ]
          },
          "statement": "For a finite quiver $Q$, let $R$ and the invertible class $\\mathbb L$ be\nas in [[def-motivic-stack-function-groups-for-quiver-representations]].\nFor dimension vectors $\\mathbf d,\\mathbf e\\in\\mathbb N^{Q_0}$ define\n$$\\chi_Q(\\mathbf d,\\mathbf e) =\\sum_{i\\in Q_0}d_i e_i- \\sum_{a\\in Q_1}d_{s(a)}e_{t(a)}.$$This is the Euler pairing for the fixed quiver representation convention: the first argument is the quotient dimension and the second is the subrepresentation dimension. It is bilinear by its displayed finite-sum formula. Let $T_Q=\\bigoplus_{\\mathbf d\\in\\mathbb N^{Q_0}}R\\,x^{\\mathbf d}$ be the free $R$-module on formal symbols $x^{\\mathbf d}$. Equip it with the bilinear multiplication$$x^{\\mathbf d}x^{\\mathbf e} =\\mathbb L^{-\\chi_Q(\\mathbf d,\\mathbf e)} x^{\\mathbf d+\\mathbf e}.$$\nThe subsequent theorem verifies associativity and the unit $x^{\\mathbf 0}$.\nThis is the Euler-twisted dimension-vector monoid algebra used as the\ntarget of the stack integration map; the formula fixes its twist convention.",
          "source_path": "items/def-quiver-motivic-quantum-torus.md"
        },
        {
          "id": "lem-finite-field-stack-groupoid-cardinality-respects-motivic-relations",
          "kind": "lemma",
          "title": "Finite-field groupoid cardinality respects the motivic stack relations",
          "deps": [
