      "items": [
        {
          "id": "def-temperley-lieb-type-a-path-spaces-and-matrix-unit-tower",
          "kind": "definition",
          "title": "Type-A path spaces and their matrix-unit tower",
          "dependency_level": 0,
          "deps": [],
          "justified_by": [],
          "statement": "Let $\\ell\\ge3$. The path graph $A_{\\ell-1}$ has vertex set $\\{0,1,\\ldots,\\ell-2\\}$ and an edge between $a$ and $b$ exactly when $|a-b|=1$. For $n\\ge0$ and a vertex $a$, let $\\mathsf P_{n,a}$ be the set of sequences\n$$\np=(a_0,a_1,\\ldots,a_n)\n$$\nwith $a_0=0$, $a_n=a$, each $a_j\\in\\{0,1,\\ldots,\\ell-2\\}$, and $|a_j-a_{j-1}|=1$ for $1\\le j\\le n$. The set is finite; it may be empty. Let $V_{n,a}:=\\mathbb C^{(\\mathsf P_{n,a})}$ be the free complex vector space with basis $\\{|p\\rangle:p\\in\\mathsf P_{n,a}\\}$, and put\n$$\nK_n:=\\bigoplus_{a=0}^{\\ell-2}\\operatorname{End}_{\\mathbb C}(V_{n,a}),\n$$\nomitting zero summands. For $p,q\\in\\mathsf P_{n,a}$, the matrix unit $E^{(n,a)}_{p,q}$ sends $|q\\rangle$ to $|p\\rangle$, sends every other path basis vector to zero, and is zero on every endpoint block other than $a$.\n\nEquip each $V_{n,a}$ with the Hermitian inner product for which its path basis is orthonormal, and equip each endomorphism algebra with the corresponding adjoint. Thus $(E^{(n,a)}_{p,q})^*=E^{(n,a)}_{q,p}$, and $K_n$ has the componentwise involution.\n\nFor $b\\sim a$, write $pb=(a_0,\\ldots,a_n,b)$ for the path obtained by appending $b$. Define the unital algebra map candidate $\\iota_n:K_n\\to K_{n+1}$ on matrix units by\n$$\n\\iota_n(E^{(n,a)}_{p,q})=\\sum_{b\\sim a}E^{(n+1,b)}_{pb,qb},\n$$\nand extend it linearly. The next local theorem proves that these assignments are injective unital $*$-homomorphisms and gives the corresponding branching rule. This is an abstract path-space tower definition; it does not assert that a particular quotient of a Temperley–Lieb algebra is isomorphic to $K_n$.",
          "provenance": {
            "statement": "literature-derived",
            "proof": "not-applicable"
          },
          "sources": {
            "references": [
              {
                "title": "David Penneys, Exercises in Quantum Algebra",
                "url": "https://people.math.osu.edu/penneys.2/archive/QuantumAlgebra.pdf",
                "locator": "§4.2, PDF pp. 31–32: the A_n Bratteli diagram and Jones tower representation setting."
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "thm-temperley-lieb-type-a-path-space-tower-branching",
          "kind": "theorem",
          "title": "The A_(ell-1) path-space tower branches by adjacent vertices",
          "dependency_level": 1,
          "deps": [
            "def-temperley-lieb-type-a-path-spaces-and-matrix-unit-tower"
          ],
          "justified_by": [],
          "statement": "Let $\\ell\\ge3$ and use the path sets, endpoint modules, matrix units, and maps $\\iota_n$ of [[def-temperley-lieb-type-a-path-spaces-and-matrix-unit-tower]]. Then each $\\iota_n:K_n\\to K_{n+1}$ is a unital injective $*$-algebra homomorphism. For every endpoint $b$, the restriction of the natural $K_{n+1}$-module $V_{n+1,b}$ to $K_n$ is\n$$\nV_{n+1,b}\\!\\downarrow_{K_n}\\cong\\bigoplus_{\\substack{0\\le a\\le\\ell-2\\\\|a-b|=1}}V_{n,a},\n$$\nwith each summand occurring once; vertices outside $\\{0,\\ldots,\\ell-2\\}$ contribute no summand.",
          "provenance": {
