        {
          "id": "def-temperley-lieb-diagram-tower-and-right-closure",
          "kind": "definition",
          "title": "Finite diagram tower inclusion and normalized right closure",
          "dependency_level": 2,
          "deps": [
            "def-temperley-lieb-diagram-category",
            "thm-temperley-lieb-diagram-category-laws",
            "def-temperley-lieb-normalized-markov-trace-by-closure"
          ],
          "justified_by": [],
          "statement": "Use the diagram algebra $\\mathrm{TL}_n(\\mathbb C,\\delta)$ and its stacking convention from [[def-temperley-lieb-diagram-category]] and [[thm-temperley-lieb-diagram-category-laws]]. For $n\\ge1$, append a rightmost vertical strand to every $(n,n)$ diagram and extend linearly; denote this map by\n$$\n\\iota_n:\\mathrm{TL}_n(\\mathbb C,\\delta)\\longrightarrow \\mathrm{TL}_{n+1}(\\mathbb C,\\delta),\\qquad x\\longmapsto x\\otimes1.\n$$\nFor a basis diagram $D:(n+1)\\to(n+1)$, join its rightmost top and bottom boundary points by an arc outside the rectangle, remove every resulting closed component with the factor $\\delta$, and retain the induced $(n,n)$ matching. Extend this **right closure** linearly as $c_n$. When $\\delta\\in\\mathbb C^\\times$, define the normalized right-closure map\n$$\nE_n:=\\delta^{-1}c_n:\\mathrm{TL}_{n+1}(\\mathbb C,\\delta)\\longrightarrow\\mathrm{TL}_n(\\mathbb C,\\delta).\n$$\nThe normalized closure traces $\\tau_n$ are those of [[def-temperley-lieb-normalized-markov-trace-by-closure]]. No positivity of $\\tau_n$ is included in this definition. The next result proves the algebraic expectation identities for $E_n$ and states precisely when it is a positive conditional expectation.\n\nWhen $\\delta\\in\\mathbb R$, equip each diagram algebra with the conjugate-linear involution that reflects a diagram across a horizontal line and conjugates coefficients. Reflection reverses stacking and fixes the loop weight, so $(xy)^*=y^*x^*$ and $1^*=1$. The positivity assertion below assumes this involution and a compatible finite-dimensional $C^*$-algebra structure.",
          "provenance": {
            "statement": "literature-derived",
            "proof": "not-applicable"
          },
          "sources": {
            "references": [
              {
                "title": "David Penneys, Exercises in Quantum Algebra",
                "url": "https://people.math.osu.edu/penneys.2/archive/QuantumAlgebra.pdf",
                "locator": "§2.1.4, PDF pp. 7–8: the right inclusion, conditional-expectation tangle, closure trace, and trace rules."
              },
