          "statement": "Take the unnormalized split p-adic Iwahori parameter $q_F=3$ (for instance, the residue-field cardinality of $\\mathbb Q_3$) and the finite type-A Hecke parameter $\\xi=i\\in\\mathbb C^\\times$. The first is positive real and greater than $1$; the second is a primitive fourth root of unity. Their quantum characteristics differ, so the parameters belong to different regimes. This calculation does not assert that the resulting affine and finite Hecke algebras are nonisomorphic or non-Morita-equivalent.",
