          "statement": "Let $E=\\mathbb R^2$ with the dot product and standard vectors $e_1,e_2$. Set\n$$\nY=\\mathbb Z(e_1-e_2)+\\mathbb Z(2e_2)=\\{(a,b)\\in\\mathbb Z^2:a+b\\text{ is even}\\},\\qquad X=\\mathbb Z e_1+\\mathbb Z\\tfrac12(e_1+e_2).\n$$\nThe displayed bases of $X$ and $Y$ are dual under the dot product. Let\n$$\n\\Phi=\\{\\pm e_1,\\pm e_2,\\pm(e_1+e_2),\\pm(e_1-e_2)\\},\n$$\nwith coroot $\\alpha^\\vee=2\\alpha$ for the short roots $\\alpha=\\pm e_i$ and $\\alpha^\\vee=\\alpha$ for the long roots $\\alpha=\\pm e_1\\pm e_2$. Choose $\\Delta=\\{\\alpha_1=e_1-e_2,\\alpha_2=e_2\\}$. The affine alcove is\n$$\n\\mathcal A_0=\\{(x_1,x_2):0<x_2<x_1,\\ x_1+x_2<1\\}.\n$$\nIts simple reflections are $s_1(x_1,x_2)=(x_2,x_1)$, $s_2(x_1,x_2)=(x_1,-x_2)$, and $s_0(x_1,x_2)=(1-x_2,1-x_1)$. The affine Iwahori–Matsumoto parameters are $q_{s_0}=q_{s_1}=2$ on the long-root walls and $q_{s_2}=3$ on the short-root wall.",
