          "statement": "Use the Wall-form Maslov convention of [[lem-maslov-index-four-lagrangian-cocycle]]. Let $B\\subseteq\\overline V\\oplus W$ be a finite-dimensional real Lagrangian relation, where the product symplectic form is $-\\omega_V\\oplus\\omega_W$. Write $B(L)=\\{w:\\exists v\\in L,(v,w)\\in B\\}$ and $B^t(Q)=\\{v:\\exists w\\in Q,(v,w)\\in B\\}$. For Lagrangians $L,P\\subseteq V$ and $Q,R\\subseteq W$,\n\n$$\\mu_V(L,P,B^t(Q))+\\mu_W(B(L),Q,R)=\\mu_W(B(P),Q,R)+\\mu_V(L,P,B^t(R)).$$\n\nConsequently, for composable Lagrangian relations $A:V_0\\to V_1$, $B:V_1\\to V_2$, $C:V_2\\to V_3$ and specified Lagrangians $\\lambda_i\\subseteq V_i$, the integer correction $m(B,A)=\\mu_{V_1}(A(\\lambda_0),\\lambda_1,B^t(\\lambda_2))$ satisfies\n\n$$m(B,A)+m(C,BA)=m(C,B)+m(CB,A).$$\n\nIt vanishes when either relation is the identity of a specified object $(V,\\lambda)$ (so the source and target specified Lagrangians agree), is additive on direct sums, and for graphs of symplectic isomorphisms $f_1,f_2$ equals $\\mu(f_2f_1\\lambda_0,f_2\\lambda_1,\\lambda_2)$. No injectivity, transversality or equal-dimension hypothesis on a general relation is imposed.",
