          "statement": "Let $\\mathcal C$ be modular with $p_\\pm=\\sum_i\\theta_i^{\\pm1}d_i^2$, $D^2=\\sum_i d_i^2$, and $\\kappa=p_+/D$. Then\n\n$$p_+p_-=D^2,\\qquad \\kappa^{-1}=p_-/D.$$\n\nThe formal Kirby color is $\\Omega=\\sum_i d_i\\,i$. A zero-framed $\\Omega$ meridian around a simple strand $j$ acts by $D^2\\delta_{j,0}$ times the identity, and a $\\pm1$-framed $\\Omega$ unknot evaluates to $p_\\pm$. Hence the surgery normalization\n\n$$\\tau(M_L)=D^{-m-1}\\kappa^{-\\sigma(B)}F(L_\\Omega)$$\n\nis invariant under adding/removing a disjoint $\\pm1$-framed $\\Omega$ unknot; it gives $\\tau(S^3)=D^{-1}$ and $\\tau(S^2\\times S^1)=1$. The same normalized graph evaluation is invariant under full framed surgery-component handle slides and colored-strand slides over surgery components, with all arbitrary exterior graph coupons retained. A topological theorem asserting completeness of these and relative moves is a separate supplier.",
