          "statement": "Assume full AC. Let $N\\cong D^2\\times S^1$ be an oriented solid torus in the interior of an oriented smooth 3-manifold, let $K$ be its core with any integral framing, and let $U$ be a small meridian of $K$ with the zero framing given by its meridian disk. Simultaneous framed surgery on $K$ and $U$ returns a solid torus diffeomorphic to $N$ by a diffeomorphism equal to the original identification on $\\partial N$. Thus inserting or removing this pair preserves the ambient manifold relative to the complement of $N$, including external collars and boundary parametrizations. An embedded colored ribbon graph avoiding $N$ is fixed. No assertion is made that a graph traversing $N$ is fixed, or that this operation belongs to a complete relative move list.",
