          "statement": "Assume full AC. Let $q$ be an index-$k$ Morse critical point in dimension $n$, $1\\le k\\le n-1$, with fixed local coordinates and descending field $f=c-|u|^2+|v|^2$, $X=(2u,-2v)$, for $(u,v)\\in\\mathbb R^k\\times\\mathbb R^{n-k}$. Let $p$ be a higher critical point of the same index. Suppose a one-parameter family of the descending attaching-sphere sections of $p$ passes through the stable section of $q$ once, at one point, and transversely in the following sense: its $k-1$ sphere-patch directions and its parameter direction map isomorphically onto the $k$ unstable directions at the event. Assume all remaining attaching data are disjoint from the chosen local passage region; retain the joining band, lower regular level, and normal framing, and assume no intervening critical point between that region and the chosen lower level.\n\nThe two framed attaching embeddings obtained by transporting below $q$, before and after this isolated passage, differ by the signed framed band sum with a parallel of the attaching sphere of $q$. For $k=1$ this replaces one foot by a parallel of the other foot of $q$ along the band. For $1\\le k\\le n-2$ this is the handle slide of the existing definition and preserves the relative diffeomorphism type with all later attaching maps carried along. In particular $n=4,k=2$ gives the framed-link slide. For $n=3,k=2$, only the stated local surface band sum with its supplied embedded band is asserted; no higher-codimension band-existence contract is imported. No generic-family existence or global trajectory-completeness assertion is made.",
          "statement_or_definition": "Assume full AC. Let $q$ be an index-$k$ Morse critical point in dimension $n$, $1\\le k\\le n-1$, with fixed local coordinates and descending field $f=c-|u|^2+|v|^2$, $X=(2u,-2v)$, for $(u,v)\\in\\mathbb R^k\\times\\mathbb R^{n-k}$. Let $p$ be a higher critical point of the same index. Suppose a one-parameter family of the descending attaching-sphere sections of $p$ passes through the stable section of $q$ once, at one point, and transversely in the following sense: its $k-1$ sphere-patch directions and its parameter direction map isomorphically onto the $k$ unstable directions at the event. Assume all remaining attaching data are disjoint from the chosen local passage region; retain the joining band, lower regular level, and normal framing, and assume no intervening critical point between that region and the chosen lower level.\n\nThe two framed attaching embeddings obtained by transporting below $q$, before and after this isolated passage, differ by the signed framed band sum with a parallel of the attaching sphere of $q$. For $k=1$ this replaces one foot by a parallel of the other foot of $q$ along the band. For $1\\le k\\le n-2$ this is the handle slide of the existing definition and preserves the relative diffeomorphism type with all later attaching maps carried along. In particular $n=4,k=2$ gives the framed-link slide. For $n=3,k=2$, only the stated local surface band sum with its supplied embedded band is asserted; no higher-codimension band-existence contract is imported. No generic-family existence or global trajectory-completeness assertion is made.",
