          "statement": "Assume AC. In dimension $d\\ge4$, a one-handle whose feet lie in the same connected lower stage can be replaced, provided its core can be closed by a joining arc to a circle with orientable normal bundle, by an interior framed circle surgery, with one $(d-2)$-handle. The resulting manifold may change, but its entire boundary, specified collar and every later attaching map are identified with the old ones. This normal-bundle condition holds for an orientation-compatible attachment in an oriented lower stage. It is necessary for a framed-circle trade: a twisted normal disk bundle has no product framing. The framing for this existence trade is the displayed product framing. Separately, surgery on a prescribed rank-three-framed circle lying in a product three-dimensional level of an oriented four-manifold, with its framing homotopic to a level rank-two framing plus the level-normal line, is represented relative to the unaffected boundary by adjoining two four-dimensional two-handles on that framed knot $K$ and a small disk-framed zero meridian $U$. The statement retains the integral framing of $K$. In a two-handle trace every interior framed circle can be put in this form by the preceding circle lemma. The pair's boundary identification is the boundary-relative local O3 identification.",
          "statement_or_definition": "Assume AC. In dimension $d\\ge4$, a one-handle whose feet lie in the same connected lower stage can be replaced, provided its core can be closed by a joining arc to a circle with orientable normal bundle, by an interior framed circle surgery, with one $(d-2)$-handle. The resulting manifold may change, but its entire boundary, specified collar and every later attaching map are identified with the old ones. This normal-bundle condition holds for an orientation-compatible attachment in an oriented lower stage. It is necessary for a framed-circle trade: a twisted normal disk bundle has no product framing. The framing for this existence trade is the displayed product framing. Separately, surgery on a prescribed rank-three-framed circle lying in a product three-dimensional level of an oriented four-manifold, with its framing homotopic to a level rank-two framing plus the level-normal line, is represented relative to the unaffected boundary by adjoining two four-dimensional two-handles on that framed knot $K$ and a small disk-framed zero meridian $U$. The statement retains the integral framing of $K$. In a two-handle trace every interior framed circle can be put in this form by the preceding circle lemma. The pair's boundary identification is the boundary-relative local O3 identification.",
