          "statement": "Assume full AC. Let $M:\\Sigma_0\\to\\Sigma_1$ be any compact oriented smooth three-bordism with its fixed product collars, boundary parametrizations and a properly embedded finite colored framed ribbon graph with actual coupon morphisms and the prescribed labeled boundary ribbons. For each connected component of $M$, fix a connected standard base $N$ with exactly that parametrized external boundary: for example the complement in $S^3$ of disjoint standard handlebodies, one of the prescribed genus for each boundary component. Keep these boundary handlebodies, their attaching parametrizations and their marked cap ribbons fixed. A closed component uses $N=S^3$. Take the finite disjoint union with this specified component partition. More generally, any fixed connected compact oriented base with the same marked boundary is allowed on each component.\n\nThere is a finite framed link $L\\subset\\operatorname{int}N$, off the protected boundary collar, an exterior representative of the given colored ribbon graph with all original coupons, and a specified orientation-preserving output identification $N_L\\to M$ retaining every boundary parametrization and collar ribbon. Here $N_L$ is the framed Dehn filling of the link exterior. For any two such presentations, the **specified** identification of their outputs is realized up to isotopy fixed on the protected collar by a finite sequence of exterior framed isotopies and the following relative moves:\n\n1. $O1$: insert or delete a split $+1$ or $-1$ framed unknot in an interior ball, with the actual filled-ball identification.\n2. $O2$: the specified framed band slide of one surgery component over another, with the full band framing and canonical local filling comparison.\n3. $O3$: insert or delete an arbitrary integer-framed knot $K$ and its small meridian $U$ with the disk framing zero; the induced filling identification is the identity outside its solid-torus support.\n4. Exterior framed colored graph isotopy and framed slides of open graph strands over the specified surgery-framed longitudes. Every original graph label, coupon morphism, attachment order, boundary ribbon and endpoint remains fixed or is transported by the recorded move map.\n\nThus the cumulative move map, with its transported graph, realizes the given marked decorated bordism, including its specified output identification. No hypothesis on any fundamental group is imposed. $O3$ is essential in this general fixed-base scope and is not silently replaced by a split Hopf pair or by $O1/O2$ alone. All supports fix the given external collars; no unproved variable-boundary slicing move list is required. Disconnected bordisms, empty input/output surfaces, closed components, empty graphs and the empty bordism are allowed, with the fixed component partition. Any integer weight and object Lagrangians of the weighted ribbon-bordism definition are retained as part of the external data; this is a presentation and move theorem, independently of the later evaluation and anomaly formulas.",
