        {
          "id": "lem-modc-internal-end-reconstruction-and-eilenberg-watts",
          "kind": "lemma",
          "title": "Right module internal ends and Eilenberg–Watts equivalence",
          "deps": [
            "def-finite-semisimple-module-category-over-fusion-category",
            "def-separable-algebra-and-bimodule-in-fusion-category"
          ],
          "statement": "Let $\\mathcal C$ be a fusion category over an algebraically closed field $k$ and $\\mathcal M$ a finite semisimple right $\\mathcal C$-module category. There is an algebra $A$ and a right module equivalence $\\mathcal M\\simeq\\operatorname{Mod}^{l}_{\\mathcal C}(A)$. This assertion does not yet assert separability. Fix the convention\n$$\\operatorname{Hom}_{\\mathcal C}(X,[m,n])=\\operatorname{Hom}_{\\mathcal M}(m\\odot X,n).$$\nOne can take $A=[m,m]$ whenever $m$ is a module generator, meaning every object of $\\mathcal M$ is a quotient of $m\\odot X$ for some $X\\in\\mathcal C$. In particular the direct sum of the simple representatives is such a generator. The multiplication is specified below. For any such algebras $A,B$, a right exact right module functor from left $A$-modules to left $B$-modules is uniquely, up to canonical isomorphism, $P\\mapsto Q\\otimes_A P$ for a $B$-$A$ bimodule $Q$. The equivalence identifies module-natural transformations with bimodule maps. No braiding is assumed.\n\nFor a finite semisimple left $\\mathcal C$-module category and a generator $m$ with every $n$ a quotient of $X\\odot m$, the left-action version is $\\operatorname{Hom}_{\\mathcal C}(X,[m,n])=\\operatorname{Hom}_{\\mathcal M}(X\\odot m,n)$ and $n\\mapsto[m,n]$ is an equivalence to right modules over $A=[m,m]$, with $[m,X\\odot n]\\cong X\\otimes[m,n]$. This version likewise does not require or assert separability.",
          "provenance": {
            "statement": "literature-derived",
            "proof": "ai-altered"
          },
          "sources": [
            {
              "title": "Etingof, Gelaki, Nikshych, and Ostrik, Tensor Categories, §§7.9–7.11",
