        {
          "id": "lem-modc-module-functors-have-adjoints-and-separable-monads-split",
          "kind": "lemma",
          "title": "Module functor adjoints and separable-monad splittings in Mod(C)",
          "dependency_level": 1,
          "deps": [
            "def-finite-semisimple-module-category-over-fusion-category",
            "def-fusion-and-multifusion-category"
          ],
          "statement": "Let $\\mathcal C$ be a fusion category over an algebraically closed field of characteristic zero, and let $\\mathcal M,\\mathcal N$ be finite semisimple right $\\mathcal C$-module categories. Every module functor $F:\\mathcal M\\to\\mathcal N$ has left and right adjoints whose adjunction units and counits are module-natural. Every separable monad in the 2-category of finite semisimple $\\mathcal C$-module categories has a separable splitting in that 2-category.\n\nHere a separable monad is $(T,\\mu,\\eta)$ with a module-natural section $\\sigma:T\\to T^2$ of $\\mu$ satisfying $T\\mu\\circ\\sigma T=\\sigma\\circ\\mu=\\mu T\\circ T\\sigma$. A separable splitting means an adjunction $L\\dashv U$ inducing this monad whose counit admits a module-natural section.",
