          "statement": "Let $\\mathcal C$ be a fusion category over an algebraically closed field $k$, let $B$ be a separable algebra object, and let $X$ be an $A$-$B$ bimodule and $Y$ a $B$-$D$ bimodule. Put $e_B=\\sigma_B\\eta_B:\\mathbf1\\to B\\otimes B$. The endomorphism\n$$p_{X,Y}=(r_X\\otimes l_Y)\\circ(1_X\\otimes e_B\\otimes1_Y):X\\otimes Y\\to X\\otimes Y$$\nis idempotent. Its image, with the induced map $q_B:X\\otimes Y\\to\\operatorname{im}(p_{X,Y})$, is the relative tensor product $X\\otimes_B Y$: for every object $Z$, composition with $q_B$ gives a bijection from morphisms $\\operatorname{im}(p_{X,Y})\\to Z$ to maps $X\\otimes Y\\to Z$ balanced over $B$. The result is independent up to a unique canonical isomorphism of the chosen splitting of $p_{X,Y}$.",
