        {
          "id": "def-fusion-two-category",
          "kind": "definition",
          "title": "Fusion 2-category",
          "dependency_level": 2,
          "deps": [
            "def-finite-semisimple-two-category",
            "def-monoidal-weak-two-category"
          ],
          "statement": "A **fusion 2-category** is a finite semisimple linear 2-category with a weak monoidal structure, a simple monoidal unit, and left and right duals for every object. For a right dual $A^\\#$ of $A$, the duality data include 1-morphisms\n$$e_A:A\\otimes A^\\#\\to I,\\qquad i_A:I\\to A^\\#\\otimes A,$$\nand invertible cusp 2-morphisms from $(e_A\\otimes A)\\circ(A\\otimes i_A)$ to $1_A$ and from $(A^\\#\\otimes e_A)\\circ(i_A\\otimes A^\\#)$ to $1_{A^\\#}$, with the associator and unitors inserted at the indicated sources and targets.\n\nHere “simple unit” means that $1_I$ is a simple 1-morphism. A pivotal or spherical enhancement is extra structure: it requires its own duality coherence and trace axioms. Neither such enhancement nor a spherical trace is included in “fusion 2-category.”",
          "provenance": {
            "statement": "literature-derived",
            "proof": "not-applicable"
