        {
          "id": "lem-fusion-category-global-dimension-is-nonzero",
          "kind": "lemma",
          "title": "Nonzero global dimension and the canonical Frobenius scalar",
          "deps": [
            "lem-canonical-fusion-category-algebra-is-frobenius",
            "lem-canonical-fusion-algebra-modules-and-tensor-sliding"
          ],
          "statement": "Let $\\mathcal C$ be a fusion category over an algebraically closed field $k$ of characteristic zero. Use left duals $i^*$ with $\\operatorname{ev}_i:i\\otimes i^*\\to\\mathbf1$ and $\\operatorname{coev}_i:\\mathbf1\\to i^*\\otimes i$. For each simple $i$, choose an isomorphism $a_i:i\\to i^{**}$ and put\n$$d_i=\\operatorname{ev}_{i^*}(\\mathrm{id}_{i^*}\\otimes a_i)\\operatorname{coev}_i,\\qquad e_i=\\operatorname{ev}_i(a_i^{-1}\\otimes\\mathrm{id}_{i^*})\\operatorname{coev}_{i^*},\\qquad |i|^2=d_ie_i.$$\nThe scalar $|i|^2$ is independent of $a_i$. The global dimension $\\operatorname{Dim}(\\mathcal C)=\\sum_i|i|^2$ is nonzero. Over $\\mathbb C$, every $|i|^2$ is a strictly positive real number. For the canonical Frobenius algebra $(K,\\mu,\\eta,\\Delta,\\lambda)$ of [[lem-canonical-fusion-category-algebra-is-frobenius]],\n$$\\lambda\\mu\\Delta\\eta=\\operatorname{Dim}(\\mathcal C)\\ne0.$$\nNo pivotal or unitary structure on $\\mathcal C$ is assumed.",
