        {
          "id": "thm-three-cochain-gauge-equivalence-2vect-g",
          "kind": "theorem",
          "title": "A normalized 3-cochain gives the gauge equivalence of 2Vect_G^omega",
          "dependency_level": 3,
          "deps": [
            "def-four-cocycle-twisted-monoidal-structure-on-2vect-g"
          ],
          "statement": "Let $\\omega,\\omega'$ be normalized 4-cocycles on a finite group $G$, and let $\\beta:G^3\\to\\mathbb C^\\times$ be a normalized 3-cochain. Define\n$$\\delta\\beta(g,h,k,l)=\\beta(h,k,l)\\beta(gh,k,l)^{-1}\\beta(g,hk,l)\\beta(g,h,kl)^{-1}\\beta(g,h,k).$$\nIf $\\omega'=\\omega\\,\\delta\\beta$, then the identity on the underlying graded 2-category, with identity tensor and unit constraints and triple-input coherence modification $\\beta(g,h,k)$, is a monoidal 2-equivalence $2\\mathrm{Vect}^{\\omega}_G\\simeq2\\mathrm{Vect}^{\\omega'}_G$. Here $H^4(G;\\mathbb C^\\times)$ means normalized multiplicative 4-cocycles modulo coboundaries of normalized 3-cochains, with trivial $G$-action on $\\mathbb C^\\times$. Within this identity-on-grading gauge family, an untwisting to $\\omega'=1$ exists exactly when $[\\omega]=0$ in this quotient.",
