        {
          "id": "lem-modc-module-deformation-complex-contracts",
          "kind": "lemma",
          "title": "Categorical separability contracts the module deformation complex",
          "dependency_level": 4,
          "deps": [
            "def-finite-semisimple-module-category-over-fusion-category",
            "def-fusion-and-multifusion-category",
            "lem-canonical-fusion-category-algebra-is-separable",
            "lem-separability-contracts-normalized-categorical-hochschild-complex"
          ],
          "statement": "Let $\\mathcal C$ be a fusion category over an algebraically closed field of characteristic zero. For finite semisimple $\\mathcal C$-module categories, the normalized deformation complexes of a fixed module action and of a fixed module functor, defined below, admit an explicit homotopy satisfying $dh+hd=\\mathrm{id}$ in every positive degree. In particular their degree-two cohomology vanishes.\n\nUse left actions initially, writing $M_X$ and $N_X$ for the action functors on $\\mathcal M$ and $\\mathcal N$. For a module functor $T:\\mathcal M\\to\\mathcal N$, use its comparisons $\\gamma_X:N_XT\\to TM_X$. Set\n$$C_T^n=\\operatorname{Nat}\\bigl((X_1,\\ldots,X_n)\\mapsto N_{X_1}\\cdots N_{X_n}T,\\ (X_1,\\ldots,X_n)\\mapsto TM_{X_1}\\cdots M_{X_n}\\bigr).$$\nHere $C_T^0=\\operatorname{Nat}(T,T)$. The zeroth coface is $(\\gamma_{X_1}M_{X_2}\\cdots M_{X_{n+1}})(N_{X_1}f_{X_2,\\ldots,X_{n+1}})$; the last coface is $(f_{X_1,\\ldots,X_n}M_{X_{n+1}})(N_{X_1}\\cdots N_{X_n}\\gamma_{X_{n+1}})$. The $j$th interior coface merges $X_j,X_{j+1}$ and transports $f$ by the specified module associators. Their alternating sum, with signs $(-1)^j$ for $0\\leq j\\leq n+1$, is $d$. Normalization means zero whenever any $X_j=\\mathbf1$, using the given unit comparisons. For $T=\\mathrm{id}_{\\mathcal M}$ these are the module-action deformation cochains. For a fixed general $T$ they are the module-functor deformation cochains.\n\nFor the right-action convention of [[def-finite-semisimple-module-category-over-fusion-category]], apply this definition to $\\mathcal C^{\\mathrm{rev}}$ and reverse the variable list: $M_X(m)=m\\odot X$, and the action comparison is $M_YM_X\\to M_{X\\otimes Y}$. In particular degree two is the space of natural endomorphisms of $(X,Y)\\mapsto M_YM_X$, after transporting through the fixed action comparisons.",
          "provenance": {
            "statement": "literature-derived",
            "proof": "ai-altered"
          },
          "sources": [
            {
              "title": "Etingof, Gelaki, Nikshych, and Ostrik, Tensor Categories, Sections 7.22 and 9.1",
              "url": "https://math.mit.edu/~etingof/egnobookfinal.pdf"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "lem-modc-module-functor-categories-are-finite-semisimple",
          "kind": "lemma",
          "title": "Module-functor categories are finite semisimple",
          "dependency_level": 4,
          "deps": [
