          "statement": "For finite semisimple right $\\mathcal C$-module categories $\\mathcal M,\\mathcal N$ over a fusion category over an algebraically closed field $k$ of characteristic zero, the category $\\operatorname{Fun}_{\\mathcal C}(\\mathcal M,\\mathcal N)$ of module functors and module-natural transformations is finite semisimple. In addition, evaluation at the tensor unit identifies $\\operatorname{Fun}_{\\mathcal C}(\\mathcal C,\\mathcal C)$ with $\\mathcal C$ and sends the identity module functor to $\\mathbf1_{\\mathcal C}$; hence the unit object of the monoidal $2$-category is simple. Here “finite semisimple” means a $k$-linear abelian category with finitely many simple isomorphism classes, finite dimensional Hom spaces, and every object a finite direct sum of simples.",
          "provenance": {
            "statement": "literature-derived",
            "proof": "ai-altered"
