            "lem-modc-module-category-rank-bound",
            "lem-modc-surjective-orbit-tangents-give-finite-orbits"
          ],
          "statement": "Assume the Axiom of Choice. Fix a fusion category $\\mathcal C$ over an algebraically closed field $k$ of characteristic zero. For each fixed possible rank of a finite semisimple right $\\mathcal C$-module category, its module structures are represented, after choosing action multiplicities, by a finite union of affine varieties of finite type. The change-of-basis group on each such variety has finitely many orbits, each open, if the degree-two normalized action-deformation cohomology vanishes at every point. This vanishing is supplied by [[lem-modc-module-deformation-complex-contracts]]. Orbits on a fixed labelled action skeleton are equivalence classes of its normalized module structures with that labelling; forgetting labels can only identify further classes. There are consequently finitely many module categories of any fixed rank and finitely many indecomposable finite semisimple module categories up to module equivalence.\n\nThe finite union over action multiplicity arrays is essential: rank alone does not specify an action functor. No algebra classification or categorical trace positivity is assumed.",
