          "statement": "Let $\\mathcal C$ be a fusion category over an algebraically closed field of characteristic zero, and let $\\mathcal M$ be a finite semisimple right $\\mathcal C$-module category. There is a separable algebra object $A$ in $\\mathcal C$ and a right $\\mathcal C$-module equivalence $\\mathcal M\\simeq\\operatorname{Mod}^{l}_{\\mathcal C}(A)$, the category of left $A$-modules fixed in [[def-separable-algebra-and-bimodule-in-fusion-category]]. The construction below fixes the right-action/internal-Hom convention, gives the internal-end multiplication and a separability section, and proves full faithfulness and essential surjectivity. With these conventions, right module functors from left $A$-modules to left $B$-modules correspond to $B$-$A$ bimodules $Q$, acting by $Q\\otimes_A-$; module-natural transformations correspond to bimodule maps.",
