          "statement": "Let $\\mathcal C$ be a braided fusion category and let $\\mathcal M\\simeq\\operatorname{Mod}^{l}_{\\mathcal C}(A)$ and $\\mathcal N\\simeq\\operatorname{Mod}^{l}_{\\mathcal C}(B)$ be finite semisimple right module categories represented by separable algebras; the left-module notation is fixed in [[def-separable-algebra-and-bimodule-in-fusion-category]]. Their relative Deligne product as fixed in [[def-modc-relative-deligne-product]] exists, is finite semisimple, and is equivalent as a right $\\mathcal C$-module category to $\\operatorname{Mod}^{l}_{\\mathcal C}(A\\otimes B)$, where the algebra product uses the braiding $c_{B,A}$. This equivalence is independent, up to canonical equivalence, of the chosen algebra presentations and supplies the object tensor product in the separable-algebra model of $\\operatorname{Mod}(\\mathcal C)$. The relative products assemble into a weak monoidal $2$-category: associators and unitors are the unique equivalences preserving the relevant universal balanced functors, the pentagon and triangle modifications obey their coherence equations, and the product is compatible with module functors and module-natural transformations.",
