          "statement": "Assume the Axiom of Choice. Let $\\mathcal C$ be a braided fusion category over an algebraically closed field of characteristic zero. The 2-category $\\operatorname{Mod}(\\mathcal C)$ of finite semisimple right $\\mathcal C$-module categories, module functors, and module-natural transformations, with monoidal product given by relative Deligne tensor product over $\\mathcal C$ (using its braiding to convert one action), is a fusion 2-category. In particular it is finite semisimple, has a simple unit, has left and right object duals, every 1-morphism has adjoints, every separable monad splits, and it has finitely many equivalence classes of simple objects.",
