              {
                "title": "John C. Baez, The Octonions, arXiv:math/0105155v4 (2002)",
                "url": "https://arxiv.org/pdf/math/0105155v4"
              }
            ]
          },
          "status": "draft",
          "definition": "Let $k$ be a field with $operatorname{char}(k)\\ne2$ ([[def-field]]) and let $J$ be a $k$-vector space ([[def-vector-space]]). A **Jordan $k$-algebra** is a bilinear product $\\circ:J\\times J\\to J$ (linear in each argument) such that $x\\circ y=y\\circ x$ and $x\\circ(y\\circ x^2)=(x\\circ y)\\circ x^2$ for all $x,y\\in J$, where $x^2:=x\\circ x$. Associativity is not required. It is **unital** if there is $1_J\\in J$ with $1_J\\circ x=x$ for all $x$."
        },
        {
          "id": "def-alternative-algebra",
