                "url": "https://www.fieldsinstitute.ca/programs/scientific/11-12/exceptional/Alb.-alg.-Ottawa-2012-Vii-new.pdf"
              }
            ]
          },
          "status": "draft",
          "definition": "Let $k$ be a field and $A$ a $k$-vector space. An **alternative $k$-algebra** is a bilinear product $A\\times A\\to A$ (linear in each argument) satisfying $x(xy)=(x^2)y$ and $(yx)x=y(x^2)$ for all $x,y\\in A$, where $x^2:=xx$. Associativity and a unit are not part of this definition."
        },
