          "definition": "A **complex associative algebra with involution** is a unital associative algebra over $\\mathbb C$ ([[def-algebra-over-a-commutative-ring]]) equipped with a conjugate-linear map $a\\mapsto a^*$ ([[def-complex-conjugate-real-imaginary-part-and-modulus]]) such that $(a^*)^*=a$, $(ab)^*=b^*a^*$, and $1^*=1$. The self-adjoint part is $A_{\\rm sa}:=\\{a\\in A:a^*=a\\}$, regarded as a real vector space."
