          "statement": "Let $V$ be a finite-dimensional real inner-product space, let $Q(v)=\\langle v,v\\rangle$, and use the plus-$Q$ Clifford algebra $\\mathrm{Cl}^{+}(V,Q)$ of [[def-clifford-algebra-of-a-quadratic-space]]. The map $\\Phi:S(V)\\to \\mathrm{Cl}^{+}(V,Q)^+$, $\\Phi(v,\\alpha)=\\bar v+\\alpha 1$ is an injective unital Jordan homomorphism onto the Jordan subalgebra $\\mathbb R1+\\bar V$. In particular, $\\bar v\\bar w+\\bar w\\bar v=2\\langle v,w\\rangle1$. The spin-factor square cone is exactly $\\{(v,\\alpha):\\alpha\\geq\\|v\\|\\}$, whose boundary is the future null cone $\\{(v,\\alpha):\\alpha\\geq0,\\ \\alpha^2-\\|v\\|^2=0\\}$ of $q(v,\\alpha)=\\alpha^2-\\|v\\|^2$."
