          "definition": "As a real vector space set $\\mathbb O:=\\mathbb H\\times\\mathbb H$, with componentwise addition and real scalar multiplication, using the quaternion algebra and conjugation of [[def-quaternions]]. Define\n\n$$\n(a,b)(c,d):=(ac-\\bar d\\,b,\\; da+b\\bar c),\\qquad \\overline{(a,b)}:=(\\bar a,-b).\n$$\n\nThe unit is $(1,0)$, and $i=(i,0)$, $j=(j,0)$, $k=(k,0)$, $\\ell=(0,1)$, with $i\\ell=(0,i)$, $j\\ell=(0,j)$, and $k\\ell=(0,k)$. This fixes the multiplication convention; the alternative laws and nonassociativity are proved in [[thm-octonions-are-alternative-but-not-associative]]."
